RISC-V Zba/Zbb/Zbs lowering fixes found while auditing perf-28's producer assumptions:
- BSWAP takes its width from the node and a 32-bit result is shifted back arithmetically (srai), so the
  int32 stays sign-extended as RV64 and perf-28 expect; BSWAP16 keeps its srli.
- slli.uw masks its shift amount to 6 bits, as genCodeForShift does.
- a | (1 << b), a ^ (1 << b) and a & ~(1 << b) with a variable index become BIT_* only for 64-bit
  operations: Zbs has no *w forms, and the 32-bit form needed the index wrapped and the result
  sign-extended again.
- ADD_UW/SH(X)ADD_UW no longer absorb a checked int->long cast, and SH(X)ADD no longer absorbs a checked
  MUL: both folds dropped the overflow check.

